======================================================SHallow copy/deep copy/ seel & Freeze=========================================
Shallow Copy (Most Confusing Topic)
    What is Shallow Copy?
    A new object is created, but nested objects still share the same reference.
    Example
    let user = {
      name: "Nazeer",
      address: {
        city: "Chennai"
      }
    };
    let copyUser = { ...user }; // shallow copy
    Memory
    user ──▶ Heap Object
              ├─ name: "Nazeer"
              └─ address ──▶ { city: "Chennai" }
    
    copyUser ─┘
    
    Modify Nested Object
    copyUser.address.city = "Bangalore";
    console.log(user.address.city); // "Bangalore" 😱
    ❗ Problem:
    address is shared
    Both objects point to same nested object
    
    | Method            | Type   |
    | ----------------- | ------ |
    | `{ ...obj }`      | Object |
    | `Object.assign()` | Object |
    | `[...arr]`        | Array  |
    | `Array.slice()`   | Array  |

Deep Copy (Correct & Safe Way):
    What is Deep Copy?
    New object
    New nested objects
    No shared references
    
    Example using structuredClone() ✅ (BEST)
    let deepUser = structuredClone(user);
    deepUser.address.city = "Hyderabad";
    
    console.log(user.address.city); // "Chennai"
    
    ✔ Fully independent
    ✔ Recommended in modern JS
    
    Other Deep Copy Methods
    🔸 JSON Method (Old but common)
    let deepCopy = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(user));
    
    ❌ Loses:
    functions
    undefined
    Date, Map, Set

Seal vs Freeze (Object Protection)
    🔒 Object.seal()
    What it does
    ✔ Cannot add new properties
    ✔ Cannot delete properties
    ❌ Can modify existing values
    Example
    let car = { brand: "BMW", price: 50 };
    
    Object.seal(car);
    car.price = 60;       // ✅ allowed
    car.color = "Black"; // ❌ not allowed
    delete car.brand;    // ❌ not allowed
    
    ❄ Object.freeze()
    What it does
    ✔ Cannot add
    ✔ Cannot delete
    ✔ Cannot modify
    Example
    let bike = { brand: "Yamaha", price: 20 };
    
    Object.freeze(bike);
    bike.price = 25;     // ❌ ignored
    bike.color = "Red"; // ❌ ignored
    
    ⚠ Important: Freeze is Shallow!
    let user = {
      name: "Nazeer",
      address: { city: "Chennai" }
    };
    Object.freeze(user);
    user.address.city = "Delhi"; // 😱 allowed
    
    ✔ Top-level frozen
    ❌ Nested object still mutable
    👉 To fully freeze → deep freeze

